  "liner": {
   "body_md": "## Setlist highlights\n\n- **I Want You (She's So Heavy)**: back after 21 archived shows (369 days) [3]\n- **banter - inviting the Shady Horns**: rare: 3 archived performances [3]\n- **banter - inviting Tash Neal**: earliest performance in the archive; legendary: the only archived performance [3]\n- **Get Back**: back after 35 archived shows (488 days); rare: 13 archived performances [3]\n- **banter - inviting George Porter Jr**: earliest performance in the archive; mythic rare: 2 archived performances [3]\n- **Check Out Your Mind**: earliest performance in the archive; rare: 3 archived performances [3]\n- **Funky Miracle**: earliest performance in the archive; mythic rare: 2 archived performances [3]\n- **banter - inviting Natalie**: earliest performance in the archive; legendary: the only archived performance [3]\n\n## The recordings\n\n- **soulive2013-03-14.cmc65.flac24** (recommended): audience recording; 20 songs; 166 min [1]\n- **soulive2013-03-14.cmc65.flac16**: audience recording; 20 songs; 166 min [2]\n\n## Around the show\n\n- Shady Horns sat in: Ryan Zoidis, James Casey and Eric Bloom, playing saxes, flute, trumpet and percussion [1]\n- Guests included Tash Neal on guitar and vocals, George Porter Jr. on bass and vocals, and John Medeski and Bill Evans [1]\n- Bowlive IV, Night 6 had no opening act; the midnight Questlove DJ set caused a curfew overrun of about 30 minutes [2]\n- Natalie Cressman joined on trombone, and Shady Horns, Tash Neal, George Porter Jr., Medeski and Evans also guested [2]\n- A higher-quality 24-bit version of this recording also exists, alongside this 16-bit one [2]\n\n## Tapers and lineage\n\n- **soulive2013-03-14.cmc65.flac24**: taped by Eric McRoberts; transferred by Eric McRoberts; source: Audience/On Stage [1]. Also: This is a 24-bit recording, catalogued as cmc65, and not meant for MP3 streaming or CD burning [1]\n- **soulive2013-03-14.cmc65.flac16**: taped by Eric McRoberts; transferred by Eric McRoberts; source: Audience/On Stage [2]",
